{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/141833-demons-conditions-and-cross-overs","id":141833,"title":"Demons, Conditions and cross overs.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-18T14:59:41-07:00","id":141833,"title":"Demons, Conditions and cross overs.","content":"Kiss of the Succubus merit states &quot;Mortals&quot; are affected. Covers are mortal. While in the cover, would the demon be addicted to the vampire's bite? <br /> <br /> Next question. If your demon is in a building with no windows or any chance an outsider could see the shift.. would they need to roll a cover check?<br /> If your cover is a homeless boy, if you move into a home does your cover degrade or is that ok?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T18:02:10-07:00","id":141959,"title":"","content":"1) No. It could unravel cover anyway assuming you don't act as expected.<br /> <br /> 2) Yes for the first one, no for the second. Covers aren't determined by some sorta concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T21:02:41-07:00","id":142052,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that changes can degrade cover, basically the rue of thumb is &quot;If this was a spy novel, would this change raise a red flag?&quot; <br /> <br /> So using your example, if a homeless boy gets put into a nice foster home, or gets adopted, completely normal. If a long lost relative shows up to take the boy in? Well that's a bit weirder, but can happen, so hopefully the demon crossed the t and dotted the i. If the demon boy just has a house out of the blue, or buys a house with a suitcase full of cash? Expect a cover hit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T08:44:48-07:00","id":143517,"title":"","content":"in the book it said that if your cover is a jerk of a boss and suddenly you started acting nicer that would be a compromise roll. Which is why I asked about the homeless thing. It does sort of imply a concept.<br /> <br /> Kiss of the Succubus merit. I was talking with some other people and the group seemed split on yes or no if the demon is affected or not. Any other input on this?<br /> <br /> Effect: All Kindred can evoke lustful, passionate reactions with a bite. The Daeva\u2019s bite is downright addicting. Her Kiss causes the Addicted Condition in mortals as well as the Swooning Condition (for Addicted, see p. 301; for Swooning, see p. 306).<br /> <br /> I suppose then this ties into The Vampire's Curse ... Is the Vampire fall then for the demon's cover as the cover is mortal??<br /> <br /> Daeva immerse themselves in the mortal world; it not only feeds them, it compels them. When Daeva choose vessels, they become obsessed. When they drink from a mortal once, they\u2019re fine. On their second and further drinks from the same source, roll Humanity. Failure causes the Persistent Dependent Condition toward the mortal (see p.302). The Condition only goes away with the mortal\u2019s death. For this reason, Daeva tend toward either remarkable promiscuity, or they cultivate massive harems and herds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T09:01:11-07:00","id":143532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/141833-demons-conditions-and-cross-overs?p=143517#post143517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in the book it said that if your cover is a jerk of a boss and suddenly you started acting nicer that would be a compromise roll. Which is why I asked about the homeless thing. It does sort of imply a concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if the Demon visibly takes anger management courses, instead of just being a different person from the day he assumed the cover? Would raise less eyebrows, wouldn't it?<br /> <br /> Every person who's homeless would like to have a roof over their heads. If the chance presents itself to the cover, why not take it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/141833-demons-conditions-and-cross-overs?p=143517#post143517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kiss of the Succubus merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>The cover assumes the conditions, not the Unchained. Shift the cover for another one and it's gone.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T10:32:42-07:00","id":143687,"title":"","content":"Thanks Ephsy. I appreciate it. So if the cover is addicted... how should the demon act?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T14:41:30-07:00","id":143884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/141833-demons-conditions-and-cross-overs?p=143532#post143532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every person who's homeless would like to have a roof over their heads. If the chance presents itself to the cover, why not take it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Big Tom, one of the Ready-Made Characters, is a Tempter who's notably chagrined at his homeless Cover and its inability to handle any sudden change in its fortunes without compromise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T15:39:03-07:00","id":143918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/141833-demons-conditions-and-cross-overs?p=143884#post143884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Big Tom, one of the Ready-Made Characters, is a Tempter who's notably chagrined at his homeless Cover and its inability to handle any sudden change in its fortunes without compromise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't have access to that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T05:07:42-07:00","id":144360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/141833-demons-conditions-and-cross-overs#post141833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kiss of the Succubus merit states &quot;Mortals&quot; are affected. Covers are mortal. While in the cover, would the demon be addicted to the vampire's bite?</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, this is more of a Vampire question than Demon. The Kiss, by default, only affects mortals. It doesn't affect any supernatural.... unless the vampire spends a point of willpower, at which point it does.<br /> <br /> So, I feel like this merit modifies what the Kiss does in general - whenever you would inflict Swooning, you also inflict Addicted. You bite a supernatural and spend a willpower point to inflict Swooning on them, then yes, I would say that KotS Addiction would affect the supernatural as well.<br /> <br /> I disagree that the Swooning and Addicted condition only affect the Cover, however. To me, that's akin to saying that damage should only affect individual covers, or that a mind control ability from a fellow supernatural only affects a cover one at a time. That's not how the game works, though. Damage carries between all forms. A demon that's been subjected to an Addiction Exploit or the Word power would be affected by those powers no matter the Cover he's in. Vampire powers should work the same way.<br /> <br /> Now, ACTING like you're addicted to the bite, or Swooning, in a Cover that shouldn't be is cause for compromise check, sure. But that doesn't mean it shouldn't still be there. This is the reason why Demons get to hide their emotional responses so well. So they can be afflicted by love and lust and desire and rage and fear towards things, but be able to not show it through an inappropriate Cover.<br /> <br /> I feel that only affecting a single cover is both detrimental to Vampire's themes, and to Demon's. Covers are just that - covers. They're basically masks you put on. This is still a single person experiencing all this. You don't suddenly fall out of love with someone just because you swap a Cover. You don't lose a mental Condition afflicted. Why should the Kiss be different?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Next question. If your demon is in a building with no windows or any chance an outsider could see the shift.. would they need to roll a cover check? </div> </div> </div>I go with StSword's take. If it would raise a red flag somehow, then compromise check. If not, then go with the flow. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If your cover is a homeless boy, if you move into a home does your cover degrade or is that ok? </div> </div> </div>Ehh... to me, that sounds like a situation that would involve a cover that's growing. As in, moving into a new home represents MORE connections, and thus justification on raising your Cover through Cover Exp. Or, rather, its something I would require raising Cover for, when next they had enough Cover exp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-21-2014, 08:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T06:25:15-07:00","id":144419,"title":"","content":"More on the vamp X demon crossover really quick - <br /> <br /> A random vamp and a random demon are at the bar. Somehow, the vamp and demon end up deciding to get a room together for an hour or two. The vampire bites the demon.<br /> <br /> Now, at this point, the vampire has absolutely no reason to suspect that the demon is, well, a demon. The vamp thinks he's biting a mortal - there's absolutely no reason for them to be spending a point of willpower. The demon will very likely be spoofing the taste of their blood as well, so the vampire should remain absolutely clueless through this entire exchange. Meanwhile, the demon will remain aware of someone biting their neck, drinking their blood, and that it feels really good, likely stunning a mortal victim. At this point, the demon has a choice - act like he knows the mortal would be reacting to the bite (as if Swooning / Addicted) or break cover and teach the vampire a lesson.<br /> <br /> If the demon chooses to remain in cover, then they will ACT like they're addicted to the Kiss. They're completely unaffected by the Conditions at this point, and they can break cover at any point they want. Until they do, the vampire should remain blissfully unaware that he's with a supernatural. That will likely be a persistent thing with that Cover from then on, up until the demon decides to break cover. After all, this is what a spy does. This is what is thematic for Demon. <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, should the demon somehow be compromised and the vampire finds out, then he's in trouble. The vampire will know he's dealing with a supernatural, and know to spend that extra effort of will to inflict the Kiss. This, too, is thematic for Demon- exposure is their bane, their weakness, just as sunlight and fire are vampire banes. They're vulnerable to people that know their secret identity.<br /> <br /> <br /> In conclusion, a demon being bit by a vampire will likely have a Cover that <i>acts</i> like they're Swooning or Addicted, though they won't have the actual Conditions. If the demon is compromised, however, all bets are off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T07:09:08-07:00","id":144450,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I really appreciate the help guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T07:45:31-07:00","id":144463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/141833-demons-conditions-and-cross-overs?p=144360#post144360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I feel like this merit modifies what the Kiss does in general - whenever you would inflict Swooning, you also inflict Addicted. You bite a supernatural and spend a willpower point to inflict Swooning on them, then yes, I would say that KotS Addiction would affect the supernatural as well.<br /> <br /> I disagree that the Swooning and Addicted condition only affect the Cover, however. To me, that's akin to saying that damage should only affect individual covers, or that a mind control ability from a fellow supernatural only affects a cover one at a time. That's not how the game works, though. Damage carries between all forms. A demon that's been subjected to an Addiction Exploit or the Word power would be affected by those powers no matter the Cover he's in. Vampire powers should work the same way.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong. Imagine if the permanent Lame condition of a cover affected them all.<br /> <br /> Damage is specific in this respect because otherwise the demons would risk compromise by shifting covers and having several Health tracks (Nevermind the extra book-keeping).<br /> <br /> One cover may be addicted to meth, the other, the CEO cover? no, not at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 05-21-2014, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T08:51:05-07:00","id":144513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/141833-demons-conditions-and-cross-overs?p=144463#post144463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wrong. Imagine if the permanent Lame condition of a cover affected them all.<br /> <br /> Damage is specific in this respect because otherwise the demons would risk compromise by shifting covers and having several Health tracks (Nevermind the extra book-keeping).<br /> <br /> One cover may be addicted to meth, the other, the CEO cover? no, not at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course that CEO cover is not addicted. But the DEMON may become addicted and then it's to his best interests to hide this addiction in other covers. Chances are, that his addict cover will get much more usage... <br /> <br /> The fact that he can perfectly pretend to be in any emotion he chooses doesn't give him immunity from physical or psychological cravings(or fears). As he may be afraid for his loved ones in a cover which doesn't even know the said people, so too he can be addicted in a cover which has never seen drugs in it's existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T10:07:11-07:00","id":144575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/141833-demons-conditions-and-cross-overs?p=144513#post144513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course that CEO cover is not addicted. But the DEMON may become addicted and then it's to his best interests to hide this addiction in other covers. Chances are, that his addict cover will get much more usage...<br /> <br /> The fact that he can perfectly pretend to be in any emotion he chooses doesn't give him immunity from physical or psychological cravings(or fears). As he may be afraid for his loved ones in a cover which doesn't even know the said people, so too he can be addicted in a cover which has never seen drugs in it's existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Explain the Lame condition, then. Or if one of the covers got cancer, the others wouldn't develop it just because of that.<br /> <br /> It would make for a pretty bitching Glitch, tho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 05-21-2014, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T13:09:44-07:00","id":144774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon the Decent Corebook</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wounds and most Conditions are part of the demon herself, not the identity. When she switches identities, any damage she\u2019s suffered or Conditions she possesses stay right where they are, which might require some clever explaining. Conditions that explicitly affect a given Cover \u2014 Notoriety, for instance \u2014 stay with that Cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>This pretty much gives all I need. Imo, addiction, vincullum and similar effects are a part of the Demon. While Lame depends on how it was aquired.. Cancer would be cover specific.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T13:20:49-07:00","id":144781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/141833-demons-conditions-and-cross-overs?p=144575#post144575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Explain the Lame condition, then. Or if one of the covers got cancer, the others wouldn't develop it just because of that.<br /> <br /> It would make for a pretty bitching Glitch, tho.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like Griautis has it right to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p.117 from DtD</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wounds and most Conditions are part of the demon herself, not the identity. When she switches identities, any damage she\u2019s suffered or Conditions she possesses stay right where they are, which might require some clever explaining. Conditions that explicitly affect a given Cover \u2014 Notoriety, for instance \u2014 stay with that Cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lame affects a specific cover. I see no reason why a Demon, a creature that feels and craves as much as any mortal, wouldn't be susceptible to addiction, especially psychologically. <br /> <br /> With regards to Kiss of the Succubus, the merit states it affects mortals. Demons have a supernatural template and therefore are unaffected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2037-iceix","name":"IceIX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T13:28:39-07:00","id":144786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/141833-demons-conditions-and-cross-overs?p=144463#post144463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wrong. Imagine if the permanent Lame condition of a cover affected them all.</div> </div> </div> </div> Your opinion, not fact. The vampire kiss and addiction are also mental effects, not just a physical responce. Cover compromises physical appearance, social connections, and a certain level of skills. That said, there is a very specific note in the book that you can have social connections that are based on the demon, and not individual covers. <br /> <br /> Lame is obviously part of one's physical appearance. That should swap with Covers. Its not something that directly targets a demon's mind like the Kiss, or any number of other powers. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Damage is specific in this respect because otherwise the demons would risk compromise by shifting covers and having several Health tracks (Nevermind the extra book-keeping). </div> </div> </div> Still sets one kind of precedent. Cover and Demon Conditions are another. <br /> <br /> Should a demon be able to ignore mental compulsions just by swapping Covers - those are Conditions, after all? I personally feel that's silly.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, remember that one's attributes don't swap as well - so, while you can switch between a teenage bookworm and professional bodybuilder, you still have a strength of 2.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One cover may be addicted to meth, the other, the CEO cover? no, not at all. </div> </div> </div> What about the DEMON himself being addicted to meth, irregardless of Cover? What about exploits that inflict addictions - are they easily shrugged off just by swapping Covers? No, of course not. <br /> <br /> There are somethings out there that are only part of one's Cover, yes. The problem here is that you seem to be asserting that ALL Conditions only affect individual Covers. This is simply not true. There are things that remain consistent between all Covers and one's Demonic Form. There are even demon-specific Conditions that specifically operate independent of Cover. Take Blown, page 119. &quot;Even if you have multiple Cover identities, the God-Machine has your frequency and the only way to lose it is to destroy the compromised cover.&quot; The Disoriented Condition is something that's purely mental, and doesn't make sense to just go away with a Cover swap.<br /> <br /> Simply put, there are clearly Conditions that, for one way or another, aren't tied to specific identities. A supernatural ability is very likely an example of such Condition sources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T13:33:50-07:00","id":144790,"title":"","content":"If a condition came with the cover or represents a social problem(or benefit), It applies to that Cover.<br /> <br /> If a condition affects the demon physically(as much as one counts), it applies across covers.<br /> <br /> EXAMPLE: If a demon picks up a drug-addict as a Cover, then he has to deal with the drug addiction in that cover. If a demon starts abusing drugs himself in any cover, then that addiction carries across Covers, because it's demon with the addiction, regardless of his tattered soul clothing.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ooh, now I want to play a demon who has a different sense-disability associated with each cover-the only time he has all his senses in action is when he's in demonic form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-21-2014, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T05:21:53-07:00","id":145567,"title":"","content":"I use the philosophy of comparing conditions to tilts in this particular respect. Physical tilts like Arm Wrack are Cover specific - because if you sprain or break your Cover's arm, and you are a sixteen limbed monstrosity from the mechanical depths of heaven, it hardly makes sense that it still applies to you in say Demonic Form (much less any other cover) - so, therefore, the question that must be asked is: Is the addiction physical or mental?<br /> <br /> Most addictions in reality are both. So, I would use ArcaneArts explanation above. If the Cover came with an addiction, and the Demon doesn't wantonly abuse the addiction while posing as the Cover, then the Demon herself would not be affected as she is not mentally addicted to the drug. She is only physically addicted to the drug because the Cover was physically addicted to the drug. (The Demon does not inherit the psychological impulses of the people they steal the lives of, I should think. But they are certainly expected to act like those people if they do acquire the Cover.)<br /> <br /> This creates an interesting premise: The idea of dangerous Covers. In these examples, at first, the Demon would surely not be addicted as it is a physical malady of the Cover. However, as she is required to live the life of the Cover in order to maintain it she would be then forced to either convincingly appear to still be addicted OR to actually take the drugs and risk becoming psychologically dependent (and gaining the Condition across all Covers.) This is made worse as the Cover has the physical addiction and so while assumed, the Demon will crave just as she would hurt with Arm Wrack.<br /> <br /> Now: If a Vampire uses this unique bite mechanic on a Demon, we have another scenario. This is applying an addiction in real-time, which means it is applying a physical dependency on the Vampire's blood to the Demon's Cover, and a psychological dependency on the Vampire to the Demon actively. But, as was earlier suggested by MCN, a Demon is still a Demon even when wearing a Cover and as a result would require the Vampire to expend Willpower to use it. If the Vampire is unaware the Demon is a Demon, then she'll need to act the part or risk compromise. If the Vampire knows the Demon is a Demon, then all she has to do is use that Willpower point.<br /> <br /> Or, so is my assumption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","user":"DesolateDolly","date":".  Creditted MCN. 05-22-2014, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T06:58:15-07:00","id":146674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceIX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/141833-demons-conditions-and-cross-overs?p=144781#post144781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With regards to Kiss of the Succubus, the merit states it affects mortals. Demons have a supernatural template and therefore are unaffected.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/141833-demons-conditions-and-cross-overs?p=145567#post145567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If the Vampire knows the Demon is a Demon, then all she has to do is use that Willpower point.<br /> <br /> Or, so is my assumption.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Does this apply to other things that state &quot;Mortal&quot; ? I cant think of anything off the top of my head...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 05-23-2014, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T10:56:09-07:00","id":146881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/141833-demons-conditions-and-cross-overs?p=146674#post146674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this apply to other things that state &quot;Mortal&quot; ? I cant think of anything off the top of my head...</div> </div> </div> </div> Check the section in Blood &amp; Smoke, under feeding, p94-95.<br /> <br /> <i>In reference to the effects of a bite, the word &quot;mortal&quot; applies to humans, ghouls, warlocks, and other things that are mostly human. Vampires, werewolves, mummies, fairies, and other things far removed from humanity are not normally subject to the Assault and the Kiss. The bite is pleasurable or unsettling; just not mechanically so.<br /> <br /> If the vampire knows she's feeding from something not human, and knows that it is otherwise immune ot the benefits of her bite, she may spend a point of Willpower to give them Scarred or Swooning Conditions as normal. Kindred are aware of this effect, and see its use as abhorrent and degrading. Kindred who rely on it with their own kind often end up ostracized or worse.</i><br /> <br /> So, being a supernatural isn't enough protection against the normal &quot;mortal only&quot; Kiss / Assault, assuming awareness on the part of the vampire. It makes sense that being a supernatural isn't enough of a protection against the Addiction power of the merit either. It makes sense, storywise, to have even werewolves and fae beings addicted to the kiss of a succubus. I can see where people would disagree, though I feel that comes down, in the end, to the usual &quot;I want my favorite splat to come out on top of this!&quot; arguments.<br /> <br /> Almost all crossover arguments come down to fangirls/boys arguing on the side of their favored supernatural. In this case, I think its moot, really, considering that, if a vampire can get the Kiss going, they're also very likely going to be able to slip a Vinculum and Blood Addiction in, which we know apply to all supernaturals now. Being addicted to a bite won't matter if they're also under a three step bond and addiction from just making out in the corner.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Its kind of important to also note that, in this case, the Kiss seems to be affecting mages by default, since they're &quot;mostly human.&quot; So, simply being a greater template, or qualifying as a supernatural, is not enough to be resistant to the Kiss (or the succubus merit either).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-23-2014, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T12:42:21-07:00","id":147016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/141833-demons-conditions-and-cross-overs?p=146881#post146881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EDIT: Its kind of important to also note that, in this case, the Kiss seems to be affecting mages by default, since they're &quot;mostly human.&quot; So, simply being a greater template, or qualifying as a supernatural, is not enough to be resistant to the Kiss (or the succubus merit either).</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my thought exactly! Covers are functionally human... It says they can grow old and die, just like any other human. I am still unsure how I should play this. My demon was bit by a vampire with Kiss of the Succubus. ( but not blood bonded ) so much back and forth! hehe.<br /> <br /> Then this begs the question. If the Demon is addicted to the bite because he is mostly human... does the daeva gain the curse for him upon further drinks?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T13:19:30-07:00","id":147064,"title":"","content":"I stand corrected. It looks like the efficacy of the power is dependent on where you place demons on the &quot;How Human is this Splat&quot; Chart. Personally, I'd say that as a being as Demons are built as ephemeral beings formed from weird science they're less human than both mages, which are affected (assuming that's what warlocks refers to) and werewolves, which aren't. However, I will concede that you can make a case that their fall makes them human enough for the power to work by default. So, ST fiat.<br /> <br /> If demons are human enough to be effected then you're just flat out addicted. If they aren't, your demon should have a chance to reflexively spoof to read as human giving the vampire no reason to use the willpower to force the effect upon you. However, your lack of addiction might lead to the vampire conducting an investigation and the unraveling of your cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2037-iceix","name":"IceIX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T18:27:57-07:00","id":147400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/141833-demons-conditions-and-cross-overs?p=147016#post147016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was my thought exactly! Covers are functionally human... It says they can grow old and die, just like any other human. I am still unsure how I should play this. My demon was bit by a vampire with Kiss of the Succubus. ( but not blood bonded ) so much back and forth! hehe.<br /> <br /> Then this begs the question. If the Demon is addicted to the bite because he is mostly human... does the daeva gain the curse for him upon further drinks?</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, like all crossover questions, it comes down to ST interpretation. I gave my thoughts a ways back. Others have come up with others. You're going to have to go with what your ST interprets. <br /> <br /> Even if you don't get the Conditions for some reason, your character could very well still become addicted to the Kiss. It still feels awesome. People become addicted to gambling and to sex. So, all I can suggest is talk to your ST and ask where you'd like this to go.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T07:50:32-07:00","id":147840,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone. Really appreciate the help and input !!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}